This local research package contains material from openai/math:

  A power improvement in the Heilbronn triangle lower bound
  Author: OpenAI
  Manuscript date: September 25, 2026
  Commit: fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb
  Repository: https://github.com/openai/math

The upstream source, PDF, comparator target, and scope note are preserved
without modification in upstream/. Their original Apache-2.0 license is
included in upstream/LICENSE and copied to LICENSE.

Local additions provide ternary and centered-sphere digit-position
constructions, local formal proofs, arithmetic certificates, checkers,
written conditional transfers, and alternative unapplied source patches.
The classical ternary construction is attributed in notes/packing.tex;
Behrend's sphere method is attributed in notes/sphere-packing.tex.
The finite sphere counting, selection, and complete packing are formalized.
The retuned d=13 packing, integer scale inequalities, and exact exponent
arithmetic are also formalized; the six-section patch remains unapplied.
The slab-cap variant restricts the classical elliptic paraboloid used
in upstream Section 5 to a slab, with a written finite-field proof.
Its revised integer scale inequalities are formalized in lean/Slab.lean.
The geometric transfer remains a written conditional argument.
No priority or unrestricted optimality claim is made.

Local author: Ivan Blinov (@littleBro).
Research, implementation and drafting used substantial OpenAI Codex assistance.
The repository organization was informed by Swapnil Jain's integer-mult-kappa
and CrocSwap's integer-mult-bounds. No mathematical results from those
integer-multiplication projects are used as assumptions here.
